  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6beef5d7-07c3-40a4-a14e-cf0cd3852783-image.png\" style=\"width: 257px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Initial height of liquid in container&#39;s of same cross section are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;respectively. Now value is opened find loss in potential energy when water level be become same</p><p>loss in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PE</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#961;Ax</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>&#961;A</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;Ag</mi><mfenced close=\"]